We are to count the number of integers $ k \in [0, 2004] $ such that $ \{k \alpha\} \in [0, c) $.

This is equivalent to counting the number of values $ k \in \{0, 1, ..., 2004\} $ for which the fractional part of $ k \alpha $ lies in $ [0, c) $.

