$$
t^* \approx 1.96
$$

(Note: This value is very close to the z-score for 94.2%, which is also approximately 1.96 due to the relatively large sample size and the fact that the t-distribution approaches the normal distribution as $ df $ increases.)

---

### **Step 4: Construct the Confidence Interval**

The point estimate of the difference in means is:

$$
\bar{x}_1 - \bar{x}_2 = 3.9 - 5.5 = -1.6
$$

The margin of error is:

$$
ME = t^* \cdot SE \approx 1.96 \cdot 0.4136 \approx 0.809
$$

So the **94.2% confidence interval** is:

$$
(-1.6 - 0.809,\ -1.6 + 0.809) = (-2.409,\ -0.791)
$$

