Let us model each card as a binary vector in $(\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z})^5$, where the $i$-th coordinate is 1 if the subset contains the $i$-th element of $S$, and 0 otherwise.

Then the problem becomes: **how many 5-element subsets of $(\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z})^5$ have sum equal to the all-ones vector?**

