### **(c) How long does it take to reduce the number of cases to 1000?**

We solve for $ t $ when $ y = 1000 $:

$$
1000 = 10000 \cdot (0.89)^t
$$

Divide both sides by 10000:

$$
0.1 = (0.89)^t
$$

Take natural logarithms on both sides:

$$
\ln(0.1) = t \cdot \ln(0.89)
$$

$$
t = \frac{\ln(0.1)}{\ln(0.89)}
$$

