We rewrite the integrand using a standard trick for rational functions:

$$
\frac{x^2}{1 + 4x^2} = \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{4(1 + 4x^2)}
$$

So the integral becomes:

$$
-2 \int \left( \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{4(1 + 4x^2)} \right) \arctan(2x) \, dx
