### **Step 1: Jacobi Iteration**

The Jacobi method updates each component using the previous iteration values:

$$
x_1^{(k)} = b_1 + \frac{1}{2} x_2^{(k-1)}, \quad x_2^{(k)} = b_2 + \frac{1}{2} x_1^{(k-1)}
$$

Let $ \varepsilon^{(k)} = [x_1^{(k)} - x_1^*, x_2^{(k)} - x_2^*]^T $. Then the recurrence becomes:

$$
\varepsilon_1^{(k)} = \frac{1}{2} \varepsilon_2^{(k-1)}, \quad \varepsilon_2^{(k)} = \frac{1}{2} \varepsilon_1^{(k-1)}
$$

This leads to the matrix form:

$$
\varepsilon^{(k)} = J^k \varepsilon^{(0)}, \quad \text{where } J = \begin{bmatrix} 0 & \frac{1}{2} \\ \frac{1}{2} & 0 \end{bmatrix}
$$

