$$
\sum_{j=r}^n \binom{j}{r} = \binom{n+1}{r+1}
$$

Thus:
- $ \sum_{j=199}^{397} \binom{j}{199} = \binom{398}{200} $
- $ \sum_{j=299}^{397} \binom{j}{299} = \binom{398}{300} $

