- **Mean**: Highly sensitive to outliers. Adding an extreme high outlier will significantly increase the mean.
- **Standard Deviation**: Also sensitive to outliers since it measures spread based on all data points.
- **Median**: Resistant to outliers. It is the middle value in a sorted dataset and is not influenced much by extreme values (especially when the dataset size is large).
- **None of the above**: Incorrect, since the median is indeed the least affected.

✅ **Answer**: **C**

