$$
\frac{(\cos x + \sin x)^2}{\cos^2 x - \sin^2 x} = \frac{1 + \sin 2x}{\cos 2x}
$$

So the original equation becomes:

$$
\frac{1 + \sin 2x}{\cos 2x} = 1 + \sin 2x
$$

