- If $ n $ is **odd**, then $ S = 0 $, so $ a(n) = n - 1 $
- If $ n $ is **even**, then $ S = \frac{n}{2} $, so $ a(n) = (n - 1) - \frac{n}{2} = \frac{n}{2} - 1 $

This gives us the formula:

$$
a(n) = 
\begin{cases}
n - 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
